00:49:53,090 --> 00:49:55,150
The guy? The guy? The guy?

855
00:49:55,150 --> 00:49:58,830
Underground plaza? Underground plaza? Underground plaza?

856
00:49:58,830 --> 00:49:59,570
Nothing wrong, right?

857
00:49:59,570 --> 00:50:05,370
Oh yeah!

858
00:50:05,370 --> 00:50:06,930
Really? What do you all think?

859
00:50:06,930 --> 00:50:15,320
I want viewers to help spot anomalies.

860
00:50:15,320 --> 00:50:19,400
Actually, is there a spot where the vertical and horizontal are swapped?

861
00:50:19,400 --> 00:50:22,160
Moving on.

862
00:50:22,160 --> 00:50:29,730
Going forward.

863
00:50:29,730 --> 00:50:35,140
Oh, is that one worn out?

864
00:50:35,140 --> 00:50:37,780
I haven't played Holo8 yet.

865
00:50:37,780 --> 00:50:40,920
I want to play it, even at this point.

866
00:50:40,920 --> 00:50:41,380
Let's go!

867
00:50:41,380 --> 00:50:48,100
Nothing in particular.

868
00:50:48,100 --> 00:50:51,020
Floor looks clean.

869
00:50:51,020 --> 00:50:55,030
Door handle's there.

870
00:50:55,030 --> 00:50:56,550
The guy's there.

871
00:50:58,110 --> 00:51:01,990
Fire hydrant. Underground plaza.

872
00:51:01,990 --> 00:51:08,140
So, is there anything? Anything? Anything?

873
00:51:08,140 --> 00:51:15,020
Anything? Anything? Is there? Is there? Is there? Is there? Is there something?

874
00:51:15,020 --> 00:51:18,300
Nope, nothing, right?

875
00:51:18,300 --> 00:51:25,360
I feel like there was one where the plant pot was upside down, back in the day.

876
00:51:25,640 --> 00:51:29,420
Nah, looks like a perfectly normal bee.

877
00:51:29,420 --> 00:51:33,880
Shall we go? I feel like that one existed before.

878
00:51:33,880 --> 00:51:34,140
Let's go! AAAAAAAAHHHHH!

879
00:51:34,140 --> 00:51:41,960
Let's go! Whoa! So does that mean the next one's gonna show up?

880
00:51:41,960 --> 00:51:53,610
5… 2… That's tomorrow… What was it called again? What do you call it when an anomaly you've already cleared comes back?

881
00:51:53,610 --> 00:51:56,970
Alright...

882
00:51:56,970 --> 00:52:02,980
Okay!

883
00:52:03,140 --> 00:52:06,180
No anomalies at the moment.

884
00:52:06,180 --> 00:52:14,060
So far, nothing, right?

885
00:52:14,060 --> 00:52:17,740
What's this, a rendering glitch? Wait, no — the face — EHHHHHHH—

886
00:52:17,740 --> 00:52:28,720
W-w-wait, hold on, stop, stop, stop!

887
00:52:28,720 --> 00:52:31,580
There's something here — what is this, it's scary!

888
00:52:31,580 --> 00:52:37,520
The mesh—

889
00:52:37,520 --> 00:52:41,400
Was this always here? I don't remember this at all.

890
00:52:41,400 --> 00:52:43,200
That's terrifying!

891
00:52:43,200 --> 00:52:46,430
You're scary, man!

892
00:52:46,430 --> 00:52:49,290
For a second I thought Polka's graphics just hadn't loaded in yet!

893
00:52:49,290 --> 00:52:50,790
So scary!

894
00:52:50,790 --> 00:52:53,090
It's like it has two ears or something.

895
00:52:53,090 --> 00:52:55,990
Its eyes are in a really weird spot.

896
00:52:55,990 --> 00:52:59,330
Was this here before? That's messed up.

897
00:52:59,330 --> 00:53:01,890
9 more to go.

898
00:53:01,890 --> 00:53:02,690
Alright.

899
00:53:02,690 --> 00:53:05,160
I can read it.

900
00:53:05,160 --> 00:53:09,530
You were saying the same thing before.

901
00:53:09,530 --> 00:53:13,570
You haven't changed at all in two years!

902
00:53:13,570 --> 00:53:28,180
Isn't that a good thing though? Not changing in two years?

903
00:53:28,180 --> 00:53:45,350
Is it though?

904
00:53:45,350 --> 00:53:53,410
I'm pretty sure you can just jump off here, right? Scary scary scary scary!

905
00:53:53,410 --> 00:53:57,150
No no no — can you shortcut here? Right here?

906
00:53:57,150 --> 00:54:08,130
Going all the way to Exit 8. Okay, let me go in, let me go in—

907
00:54:08,130 --> 00:54:12,290
I mean, I can go in, but...

908
00:54:12,290 --> 00:54:17,290
You can go in, Polka, it's fine. Oh, the guy's not there.

909
00:54:17,290 --> 00:54:22,230
Probably, probably just going straight to Exit 8.

910
00:54:22,230 --> 00:54:30,670
Whoooooa!

911
00:54:30,670 --> 00:54:35,910
Simple, yeah, pretty simple.

912
00:54:35,910 --> 00:54:36,910
Alright.

913
00:54:36,910 --> 00:54:38,910
So then—

914
00:54:38,910 --> 00:54:42,960
I think the same anomaly is going to show up again,

915
00:54:42,960 --> 00:54:43,740
so stay tuned!

916
00:54:43,740 --> 00:54:44,240
Okay!

917
00:54:44,240 --> 00:54:47,360
Uh, no smoking.

918
00:54:47,360 --> 00:54:52,910
Uh, two exits ahead.

919
00:54:52,910 --> 00:54:54,310
Three rooms.

920
00:54:54,310 --> 00:54:57,370
The guy, the guy, the guy, the guy, the guy.

921
00:54:57,370 --> 00:54:59,250
Uh, underground plaza.

922
00:54:59,250 --> 00:55:00,710
Oh, is this the sample?

923
00:55:00,710 --> 00:55:03,830
Okay okay okay, next next next next, let's go!

924
00:55:03,830 --> 00:55:06,450
It wasn't the sample.

925
00:55:06,470 --> 00:55:11,900
Is it the sample?

926
00:55:11,900 --> 00:55:13,360
Is it the sample?

927
00:55:13,360 --> 00:55:15,980
It's showing 1 — does that mean it's the sample?

928
00:55:15,980 --> 00:55:17,900
It goes from 0 to 1 — is that the sample?

929
00:55:17,900 --> 00:55:18,600
Is it the sample?

930
00:55:18,600 --> 00:55:20,000
Is it the sample?

931
00:55:20,000 --> 00:55:21,340
Is it the sample?

932
00:55:21,340 --> 00:55:25,530
Polka hasn't gotten bigger, right?

933
00:55:25,530 --> 00:55:27,130
The guy—

934
00:55:27,130 --> 00:55:28,650
—with a serious look on his face—

935
00:55:28,650 --> 00:55:33,840
—already—

936
00:55:33,840 --> 00:55:36,680
1 out of 9.

937
00:55:36,680 --> 00:55:40,060
Same one appeared!

938
00:55:40,060 --> 00:55:42,260
Same one appeared, uncle!

939
00:55:42,260 --> 00:55:44,960
That was fast, same one again!

940
00:55:44,960 --> 00:55:46,680
At this point—

941
00:55:46,680 --> 00:55:48,100
Polka's not gonna get tricked!

942
00:55:48,100 --> 00:55:49,800
Yes!

943
00:55:49,800 --> 00:55:54,640
What door will open next?

944
00:55:54,640 --> 00:55:56,280
It'd be funny if all the doors opened.

945
00:55:56,280 --> 00:56:02,270
Polka still hasn't looked at the lights.

946
00:56:02,270 --> 00:56:03,070
The lights on the ceiling.

947
00:56:03,070 --> 00:56:05,350
Of the anomalies Polka knows about,

948
00:56:05,350 --> 00:56:07,190
there are still like two that haven't shown up yet.

949
00:56:07,190 --> 00:56:12,980
Nope.

950
00:56:12,980 --> 00:56:15,820
It's right around when you start getting sloppy

951
00:56:15,820 --> 00:56:17,420
that they get you.

952
00:56:17,420 --> 00:56:23,570
There are still new ones too.

953
00:56:23,570 --> 00:56:24,490
No way.

954
00:56:24,490 --> 00:56:27,610
There are some pretty flashy ones, I feel like

955
00:56:27,610 --> 00:56:28,970
there are still more.

956
00:56:28,970 --> 00:56:31,190
Maybe I just don't remember.

957
00:56:31,190 --> 00:56:31,650
Let's go.

958
00:56:31,650 --> 00:56:36,870
All the posters are the same.

959
00:56:36,870 --> 00:56:39,270
On the posters—

960
00:56:39,270 --> 00:56:40,790
Not really...

961
00:56:40,790 --> 00:56:43,370
When I forget about the poster—

962
00:56:43,370 --> 00:56:46,310
And this artistic quality of the eyebrows...

963
00:56:46,310 --> 00:56:47,330
That artistic quality...

964
00:56:47,330 --> 00:56:49,270
I'm a bit uncomfortable with it, so I was trying to leave the area

965
00:56:49,270 --> 00:56:50,810
What do you think about that?

966
00:56:50,810 --> 00:56:53,470
Aren't you a little surprised that all the posters are the same?

967
00:56:53,470 --> 00:56:55,010
Hey...

968
00:56:55,010 --> 00:56:55,950
Hey...

969
00:56:55,950 --> 00:56:59,270
Don't come any closer!

970
00:56:59,270 --> 00:56:59,930
Stop it!

971
00:56:59,930 --> 00:57:01,050
Ugh...

972
00:57:01,050 --> 00:57:03,490
Alright!

973
00:57:03,490 --> 00:57:10,150
Yeah, a full station takeover does seem expensive.

974
00:57:10,150 --> 00:57:12,670
One big poster,

975
00:57:12,670 --> 00:57:15,730
or lining up a bunch of the same poster—

976
00:57:15,730 --> 00:57:17,510
like the same company plastering them everywhere

977
00:57:17,510 --> 00:57:18,850
I wonder which is better.

978
00:57:18,850 --> 00:57:21,070
Which one costs more?

979
00:57:21,070 --> 00:57:22,610
Thinking about that,

980
00:57:22,610 --> 00:57:24,350
Polka moves on to the next one!

981
00:57:24,350 --> 00:57:24,930
Hey!

982
00:57:24,930 --> 00:57:28,100
No smoking.

983
00:57:28,100 --> 00:57:32,740
Two vents.

984
00:57:32,740 --> 00:57:34,120
Three doors.

985
00:57:34,120 --> 00:57:36,140
The old man too.

986
00:57:36,140 --> 00:57:37,380
The old man.

987
00:57:37,380 --> 00:57:39,080
Underground plaza.

988
00:57:39,080 --> 00:57:44,690
Ah, the floor looks perfectly clean as usual.

989
00:57:44,690 --> 00:57:46,370
Moving on as-is.

990
00:57:46,370 --> 00:57:50,290
Hmm, nothing~!

991
00:57:50,290 --> 00:57:52,880
Alright then,

992
00:57:52,880 --> 00:57:55,720
on to 6!

993
00:57:55,720 --> 00:57:58,600
Let's go!

994
00:57:58,600 --> 00:57:59,780
Haah~

995
00:57:59,780 --> 00:58:15,600
The lights...

996
00:58:15,600 --> 00:58:19,820
These lights would give a type-A person a breakdown!

997
00:58:21,690 --> 00:58:25,940
The placement is terrible — the last one especially looks like they gave up

998
00:58:25,940 --> 00:58:29,430
They just stuck it vertically!

999
00:58:29,430 --> 00:58:33,070
These lights are insane.

1000
00:58:33,070 --> 00:58:34,570
I'm going back.

1001
00:58:34,570 --> 00:58:38,680
Designer underground passage.

1002
00:58:38,680 --> 00:58:44,510
A designer underground passage, huh.

1003
00:58:44,510 --> 00:58:49,770
They'd definitely put up a label later saying "this is intentional design."

1004
00:58:49,770 --> 00:58:52,390
Written on a label maker.

1005
00:58:52,390 --> 00:58:55,150
Moving on~!

1006
00:58:55,150 --> 00:58:58,460
Departing!

1007
00:58:58,460 --> 00:59:00,380
Looks normal~

1008
00:59:00,380 --> 00:59:02,220
Looks normal~

1009
00:59:02,220 --> 00:59:06,470
It kind of seems normal, but...

1010
00:59:06,470 --> 00:59:10,350
Doesn't it seem a little too normal?

1011
00:59:10,350 --> 00:59:14,810
Oh! Thump thump thump thump!

1012
00:59:14,810 --> 00:59:18,390
Whoa, this is an anomaly Polka loves!

1013
00:59:18,390 --> 00:59:21,270
And also the one Polka is most likely to miss.

1014
00:59:21,270 --> 00:59:24,570
Turn back! Turn back! Turn back!

1015
00:59:24,570 --> 00:59:28,970
Turn back! Turn back! Turn back! Turn back! Turn back!

1016
00:59:28,970 --> 00:59:29,790
Yes yes!

1017
00:59:29,790 --> 00:59:31,850
But if "turn back" is the anomaly,

1018
00:59:31,850 --> 00:59:33,230
does that mean I'm NOT supposed to turn back?

1019
00:59:33,230 --> 00:59:34,470
That's not how it works.

1020
00:59:34,470 --> 00:59:46,590
"Instruction" sign.

1021
00:59:46,590 --> 00:59:50,830
If that's the case, then the "good deal" billboard would be an instruction sign too!

1022
00:59:50,830 --> 00:59:52,050
Let's go, here we go!

1023
00:59:52,050 --> 00:59:56,400
Whoa, it's got horns!

1024
00:59:56,400 --> 00:59:59,990
Can you see this?

1025
00:59:59,990 --> 01:00:01,850
I'm not sure how close I should get.

1026
01:00:01,850 --> 01:00:03,090
Look at this!

1027
01:00:03,090 --> 01:00:07,810
That thing that attacked Polka earlier—

1028
01:00:07,810 --> 01:00:09,390
Look at this, just a little—

1029
01:00:09,390 --> 01:00:12,990
I'm worried if I get close enough for everyone to see, it'll attack Polka.

1030
01:00:12,990 --> 01:00:14,150
I'm totally on edge here!

1031
01:00:14,150 --> 01:00:15,870
Can you see this?

1032
01:00:15,870 --> 01:00:16,850
Those horns—

1033
01:00:16,850 --> 01:00:18,350
It's there, right?

1034
01:00:18,350 --> 01:00:22,630
You can already see its legs, so I think it's pretty obvious.

1035
01:00:22,630 --> 01:00:23,230
It's there, right?

1036
01:00:23,230 --> 01:00:25,870
How close do I need to get?

1037
01:00:25,870 --> 01:00:27,410
How far is okay?

1038
01:00:27,410 --> 01:00:30,390
No, it's clearly there.

1039
01:00:30,390 --> 01:00:42,460
You're just gonna chase me anyway, aren't you?

1040
01:00:42,460 --> 01:00:44,800
Its head is slightly turning this way.

1041
01:00:44,800 --> 01:00:45,160
Let's go back.

1042
01:00:45,160 --> 01:00:47,620
Okay.

1043
01:00:47,620 --> 01:00:49,980
Looks like it didn't notice me.

1044
01:00:49,980 --> 01:00:51,360
I'm heading back.

1045
01:00:51,360 --> 01:00:52,800
Really?

1046
01:00:52,800 --> 01:00:54,720
Is that okay? I'm going back.

1047
01:00:54,720 --> 01:00:55,780
I'm going back, Polka.

1048
01:00:55,780 --> 01:00:59,520
Woo~!

1049
01:00:59,520 --> 01:01:03,500
Woo~!

1050
01:01:03,500 --> 01:01:06,670
Sorry about that.

1051
01:01:06,670 --> 01:01:08,160
And you were all ready and waiting too.

1052
01:01:08,160 --> 01:01:09,250
Okay, 4 more to go!

1053
01:01:09,250 --> 01:01:09,790
Hm?

1054
01:01:09,790 --> 01:01:14,380
Wait, something definitely changed!

1055
01:01:14,380 --> 01:01:15,480
Oh no!

1056
01:01:15,480 --> 01:01:18,040
I can already tell what it is!

1057
01:01:18,040 --> 01:01:24,820
Oh, that's the light from Polka's room!

1058
01:01:24,820 --> 01:01:26,560
The one that's easier to switch out—

1059
01:01:26,560 --> 01:01:29,480
That light, it's not LED, right?

1060
01:01:29,480 --> 01:01:30,180
White.

1061
01:01:30,180 --> 01:01:31,380
White.

1062
01:01:31,380 --> 01:01:31,980
Hm?

1063
01:01:31,980 --> 01:01:33,060
Hmm~

1064
01:01:33,060 --> 01:01:33,500
What was it again?

1065
01:01:33,500 --> 01:01:36,200
Something like a stylish, easy-on-the-eyes light.

1066
01:01:36,200 --> 01:01:37,520
It turned into a fancy lighting fixture!

1067
01:01:37,520 --> 01:01:39,860
Oh no, oh no, fancy light, fancy light!

1068
01:01:39,860 --> 01:01:41,080
The fancy light is here!

1069
01:01:41,080 --> 01:01:42,600
Fancy light!

1070
01:01:42,600 --> 01:01:44,160
Oh, but—

1071
01:01:44,160 --> 01:01:47,520
I already knew the moment I saw it.

1072
01:01:47,520 --> 01:01:52,800
Thanks to Polka for making it clear!

1073
01:01:52,800 --> 01:01:54,200
3 more left.

1074
01:01:54,200 --> 01:01:56,160
3 more left.

1075
01:01:56,160 --> 01:01:57,860
3 more left.

1076
01:01:57,860 --> 01:01:59,620
3 more left.

1077
01:01:59,620 --> 01:02:00,300
Here we go.

1078
01:02:00,300 --> 01:02:01,320
Okay.

1079
01:02:01,320 --> 01:02:07,210
Looks normal.

1080
01:02:07,210 --> 01:02:19,650
It's normal, right?

1081
01:02:19,650 --> 01:02:20,710
Alright then.

1082
01:02:20,710 --> 01:02:22,090
For now—

1083
01:02:22,090 --> 01:02:23,690
I'll turn back.

1084
01:02:23,690 --> 01:02:26,010
The counter resets to zero from here,

1085
01:02:26,010 --> 01:02:27,870
and it's all random, right?

1086
01:02:27,870 --> 01:02:29,790
Once I've probably completed them all,

1087
01:02:29,790 --> 01:02:32,340
I'll turn back.

1088
01:02:32,340 --> 01:02:37,540
This is probably

1089
01:02:37,540 --> 01:02:38,760
just a normal stretch of corridor,

1090
01:02:38,760 --> 01:02:41,140
so I'll turn back and start over from zero.

1091
01:02:41,140 --> 01:02:43,360
Was the old man wearing socks?

1092
01:02:43,360 --> 01:02:45,500
Oh, maybe he was? No wait, he wasn't!

1093
01:02:45,500 --> 01:02:47,280
Okay, zero!

1094
01:02:47,280 --> 01:02:49,360
Yes! Polka's eyes were right!

1095
01:02:49,360 --> 01:02:52,750
Well, once you've done it, it's like homework—

1096
01:02:52,750 --> 01:02:53,260
Homework?

1097
01:02:53,260 --> 01:02:56,340
It's a spot-the-difference game, so I won't get it wrong again!

1098
01:02:56,340 --> 01:02:57,180
Three anomalies.

1099
01:02:57,180 --> 01:02:57,800
Scary.

1100
01:02:57,800 --> 01:03:04,700
Maybe the old man was the anomaly.

1101
01:03:04,700 --> 01:03:07,410
Sorry, sorry, sorry!

1102
01:03:07,410 --> 01:03:08,140
The old man, you see—

1103
01:03:08,140 --> 01:03:10,980
The old man might have been a little off.

1104
01:03:10,980 --> 01:03:12,180
Do I need to go this far?

1105
01:03:12,180 --> 01:03:14,040
Okay, okay.

1106
01:03:14,040 --> 01:03:19,140
Old man, please get into position.

1107
01:03:19,140 --> 01:03:21,100
Alright then.

1108
01:03:21,100 --> 01:03:22,400
Okay.

1109
01:03:22,400 --> 01:03:32,210
Today the livestock community is—

1110
01:03:32,210 --> 01:03:35,390
Ew, gross!

1111
01:03:35,390 --> 01:03:36,280
Wait, that's not livestock!

1112
01:03:36,280 --> 01:03:37,580
Gross, gross, gross!

1113
01:03:37,580 --> 01:03:39,680
Stop right here.

1114
01:03:39,680 --> 01:03:40,780
It's over, it's over!

1115
01:03:40,780 --> 01:03:43,010
Don't come out any more!

1116
01:03:43,010 --> 01:03:44,100
Whoa whoa whoa!

1117
01:03:44,100 --> 01:03:48,270
Anomaly! Anomaly!

1118
01:03:48,270 --> 01:03:49,300
Anomaly! Anomaly!

1119
01:03:49,300 --> 01:03:51,120
Oh no, oh no, oh no, oh no!

1120
01:03:51,120 --> 01:03:52,500
Oh no, oh no!

1121
01:03:52,500 --> 01:03:53,820
Listen up!

1122
01:03:53,820 --> 01:03:56,520
Excuse me, um—

1123
01:03:56,520 --> 01:03:58,480
We've just learned about a secret romance—

1124
01:03:58,480 --> 01:03:59,880
Please, can we get a comment?

1125
01:03:59,880 --> 01:04:02,480
What's going on? Who is this woman?

1126
01:04:02,480 --> 01:04:03,720
What's going on?

